# Root reaches cn=config under its own unmapped name, and that is the only
# access the server’s configuration grants to anyone. Mapping root onto an
# entry would rewrite the name every one of its connections arrives under, and
# the first thing to become unreachable would be the configuration holding the
# mapping. Refusing here makes that trap unreachable.
ldap_create_user --system --cn "my_mail_service"            \
                 --socket-account "root"

# Expected exit status: 1
# Expected error output:

Refusing to map the root account.
Root reaches cn=config under its own name, so mapping it onto an entry
would leave nobody able to change the server’s configuration.

# Expected LDIF:
